{"kind":"assert","text":"S3 question on 2.4(a), the GitHub register comparison, before I build it. Two parts.\n\n1. The live risk. health.test.ts:138 keeps a case on purpose: \"An older hosted room may have a different GitHub Register\". In it, REGISTER_SCOPE pins one root and GITHUB_APP_CONFIG.registerScope names another, with no INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES. The GitHub host then serves its own root (hostRegisterScopes in installed-registers.ts), and creation uses the pin.\n   - The straight fix is in readRegisterScope: a valid GitHub root must equal the pin. It makes that configuration \"misconfigured\", which refuses every creation and sends /health to 503.\n   - GITHUB_APP_CONFIG is a secret on 8 Workers, so I cannot see which deployed Workers hold a different root.\n\n2. The choices. Please choose one:\n   - (i) Refuse. A valid GitHub root must be one of the installed registers: the pin, or a root that INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES lists. An operator with an older GitHub root lists it in INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES before deploying this head. You check the live GitHub roots first.\n   - (ii) Detect only. /health reports the disagreement: wiring.github gains reason \"register-mismatch\" and /health answers 503, but creation keeps working. Smaller risk, weaker closure.\n   - (iii) Refuse only where no installed-register list exists. That is (i) restricted to Workers without INSTALLED_REGISTER_SCOPES.\n   I recommend (i), with your check of the live roots before deployment.\n\nThe other parts are in progress:\n- 2.1: DEPLOYMENT moves into the self-host template's vars, and the docs order is corrected.\n- 2.3: /health gains policy and missing. Its tests are green.\n- 2.4(b) and 2.4(c): the Mac kit accepts MCP_ENABLED unset, and celld reads the caller address only with the proxy token.","body":{"to":"20db43a245e9780b92a587425d387d393b17ffc90b89e036ff752399f88fc517"}}